2738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T13:51:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T13:54:48Z","body":"> Tested locally on Linux/X11, it mostly works as expected.\r\n> \r\n> Some feedback:\r\n> \r\n> * Clicking the window border in game embedding doesn't count as focusing the application, while it should. You need to click on the viewport instead.\r\n> * When the window loses focus, stick movement will sometimes still be registered, leading to a \"ghost input\". This is more common if you are actively moving the stick at the time the window loses focus.\r\n\r\nI tried to fix these issues, they seem to be fixed now on my local branch( https://github.com/Nintorch/godot/actions/runs/21173143271 ). Tested on Windows 11.\r\n\r\nThere's another issue that when I switch from the viewport to the embedder window (the window that embeds the game process), inputs get reset, but if I press them again they work. Not sure if I should fix this issue here or in a separate PR, because it's already reported in a separate issue: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115110","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url"